      "content": "Random failures that occur so quickly they don't register in your logs could indeed hint at issues at the OS or hardware level. To get to the root of this, consider running a hardware diagnostics tool to check for failing components, like RAM or hard disk sectors. You can use tools such as memtest86+ for memory and S.M.A.R.T. monitoring for hard drives to detect any hardware failures. On the OS side, consider system logs outside of Jenkins, such as audit trails or broader system monitoring tools that can capture detailed system events including kernel panic logs or hardware interrupts, which might hint at rare interference. It's also advisable to test the hardware on different OS environments to rule out OS-specific issues, or use a virtual machine snapshot feature to roll back to a clean state if intermittent problems arise at the hardware level.",
